WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:08.220
- I love my wife but I'm gay.

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:10.470
Should I come out now?

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:11.853
Yes or no?

00:00:12.857 --> 00:00:15.930
(pensive music)

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:17.730
- [Director] We brought
together a group of strangers

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:19.140
to help an anonymous person

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:21.450
make one of their toughest decisions.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:23.690
- My wife is the most
important person in my life

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:26.413
and I would never wanna
do anything to hurt her

00:00:27.257 --> 00:00:29.057
but I'm also gay.

00:00:29.057 --> 00:00:32.193
So I'm not sure how to approach it

00:00:32.193 --> 00:00:33.573
or even how to come out.

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:36.180
- [Director] After hearing
the group's advice,

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.790
which choice will this person make?

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:40.617
This is "The Dilemma".

00:00:41.502 --> 00:00:42.413
(air whooshing)

00:00:42.413 --> 00:00:45.163
(metal clanking)

00:00:54.833 --> 00:00:56.070
(air whooshing)
(tone beeps)

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.270
- How long into the relationship

00:00:57.270 --> 00:00:58.720
did you realize you were gay?

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:02.553
- I knew before I got married.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.210
- How did you meet your partner?

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:08.340
- We grew up in the
same community together.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:11.280
We started off as friends,
then best friends,

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:13.620
and it grew from there.

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:16.120
- Is your partner supportive
of everything you do?

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:20.160
- In our viewpoints on religion, yes.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:23.073
In terms of supporting
the LGBT community, no.

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:26.220
- So religion is a big cornerstone

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:28.170
of your guys' relationship?

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:30.180
- We both grew up in the
same religious community

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:33.870
so we both grew up with the same values

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:37.550
and the same social guidelines, so yes.

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:39.690
- Do you think your wife knows you're gay?

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:40.592
- No, she doesn't.

00:01:40.592 --> 00:01:41.700
(tense music)

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:42.720
- [Director] What was the main reason

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:44.820
as to why you went to the yes side?

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:46.590
- I have a few family members

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:49.110
in the LGBTQ+ community.

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:50.730
I know all their experiences coming out

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:52.410
have been positive,

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:53.460
at least in the long run.

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:55.830
I really thought to myself
about him coming here,

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:58.050
wanting to, you know, share his truth

00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:59.820
and speak to us about it.

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:01.980
I knew that it's about time.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:03.630
It's starting to boil over

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:04.724
and he needs to come out.

00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:05.580
(air whooshing)
(tone beeps)

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:07.350
- What was your reasoning
for marrying a woman

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:09.390
even though you knew you were gay?

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:11.852
- I thought that if I got married

00:02:11.852 --> 00:02:13.827
that it would change me

00:02:13.827 --> 00:02:16.200
and that I could become straight.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.810
- What are your intentions in life

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:20.910
and how do you wanna feel about your life?

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:24.030
- I wanna be truthful

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:27.030
but I also don't wanna hurt
the people surrounding me.

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:29.130
I'm a very honest person.

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:30.540
I don't lie (chuckles)

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:34.470
so the fact that I'm basically
living a lie right now

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:37.080
gives me a lot of anxiety and depression.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:41.100
But I know if I came out suddenly

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:42.425
it would devastate her.

00:02:42.425 --> 00:02:43.620
(tense music)

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:45.180
- The thing is, I'm bisexual

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:47.790
and I would've never said anything

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:49.920
if I ended up falling in love with a man

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:51.690
and everything worked out.

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:54.360
And I fell in love with a woman

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:57.630
and I didn't wanna hide anymore.

00:02:57.630 --> 00:03:00.146
Being your authentic self is my principle.

00:03:00.146 --> 00:03:00.979
(air whooshing)
(tone beeps)

00:03:00.979 --> 00:03:03.270
- So is there an expected fallout

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:05.160
that extends beyond just the relationship

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:06.000
of you and your wife?

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.700
Like, is it more than just
your guys' relationship

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:09.753
that's at stake?

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:12.360
- My job is tied to the church

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:14.370
so I could potentially lose my job.

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:16.950
I would most likely lose my family,

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:18.450
my friends, my wife.

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:20.070
I would lose everything basically.

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:21.933
I would have nothing and no support.

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:27.480
- Are we the only people
who know about this?

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:29.402
- I've never told anyone.

00:03:29.402 --> 00:03:30.600
(air whooshing)

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:33.090
- [Director] Just based
on this information now,

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:36.782
you guys can switch to the
other side if you want.

00:03:36.782 --> 00:03:39.949
(indistinct speaking)

00:03:41.581 --> 00:03:44.248
- [Levels] I don't know where...

00:03:46.687 --> 00:03:48.716
(Levels chuckles)

00:03:48.716 --> 00:03:51.000
(tense music)

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.930
- He was explaining what's at stake

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:56.610
if he comes out immediately.

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:58.050
Because of that, the
more I thought about that

00:03:58.050 --> 00:03:59.100
the more I was like, you know what,

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:02.010
he's gonna be losing literally
everything because of this.

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:04.350
So I feel like he needs
to have some sort of plan

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:05.730
in motion first.
(air whooshing)

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:08.070
- The reason I said no, I'm bisexual.

00:04:08.070 --> 00:04:09.540
Same as you it took me a cool minute

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:11.370
to kinda come to terms with that.

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:14.040
So it's like, I look more at am I safe?

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:16.020
If you do, gone.

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:18.120
You could lose a lot of
things that you've built up

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:19.800
on this foundation.

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:22.830
- Have you at all considered
reaching out to therapy

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:26.370
or some sort of counseling to
help you through this process?

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:28.200
- In the community I live in,

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:31.050
it's a little bit hard to find counseling.

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:33.360
I live in a more rural area

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:36.095
so the majority of counselors

00:04:36.095 --> 00:04:37.773
are based through the church.

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:41.190
- Can you tell me a little bit more

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:43.230
about your relationship with God?

00:04:43.230 --> 00:04:45.450
And has there been moments

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:49.143
where you've personally
experienced him guide you?

00:04:49.997 --> 00:04:53.400
- Yeah, I would say faith
has been a deciding factor

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:56.130
in all things that I do in my life

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:58.680
and that I don't follow God blindly.

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:00.930
I've felt him work in my life before.

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:04.143
So for me, it's a real
relationship that I have.

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:08.070
And it's the most important
relationship I have.

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:10.056
God goes before everything else.

00:05:10.056 --> 00:05:11.280
(tense music)

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:14.640
- Faith is just a huge
factor for my truth.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:17.490
To me, that's what I resonated the most.

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:19.860
So I wanted to be that representation

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:23.040
of like, hey, if you just
go in with blind faith,

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:24.254
it could still work out.

00:05:24.254 --> 00:05:25.350
(air whooshing)
(tone beeps)

00:05:25.350 --> 00:05:29.850
- If you show who you really
are to somebody, to anybody,

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:32.040
they're gonna show you who they are

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:33.510
like 100% of the time.

00:05:33.510 --> 00:05:35.490
And if you're surrounding
yourself with people

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:37.950
who are kind of not in support

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:39.510
of the person that you really are,

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:41.010
then that's not a healthy
situation to be in

00:05:41.010 --> 00:05:44.250
and I think he should
100% come out, like today.

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:46.020
- I'm bisexual. Took me a cool minute.

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:47.760
One of my, (chuckles)
I'm not gonna name names.

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:50.550
I'll say a family member told my parents.

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:51.810
It gave me a lot of anxiety.

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:53.100
It was like, am I gonna get kicked out?

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:54.540
I'm gonna stay here.
Are they upset with me?

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:55.800
It was very much like, okay, whatever,

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:57.000
I don't wanna talk to you right now.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:58.530
And it's like I know coming out,

00:05:58.530 --> 00:06:00.270
everyone's like, do it, do it, it's great.

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:01.200
You'll feel better.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:04.050
But for me coming out was,
it made me feel worse.

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:05.760
'Cause I'm like, I live my truth

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:08.700
but it didn't make me feel
the way I wanted to feel.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:11.580
- I believe that everybody
should live their truth.

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:14.460
You're not emotionally
responsible for anybody.

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:16.680
You don't owe anybody your life.

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:18.870
You be you and they'll
figure out how to be them.

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:20.250
- I think it's different.

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:21.780
Like you were saying
you're not responsible

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:24.030
for other people's feelings, but it is,

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:25.800
I know the guilt that I would feel

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:28.050
as a husband to be hiding
something from my wife

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:29.550
is like horrible.

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:31.380
- Yeah, 'cause like let's also not forget

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:32.280
that they are married.

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:33.420
They have vows.
- Yeah. (chuckles)

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:34.810
- And part of those vows-
- And a lot is asked of that.

00:06:34.810 --> 00:06:35.913
- is to tell the truth,

00:06:35.913 --> 00:06:36.780
you know what I mean?
- Yeah.

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:40.140
- Because you're taking away
another person's ability

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:42.660
to live in reality and that's wrong.

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:43.980
- Yes.
- I do wanna point out

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:45.270
that I'm not necessarily saying

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:47.670
that he should wait years to come out.

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:48.503
I'm just saying maybe
- Oh no,

00:06:48.503 --> 00:06:50.190
don't do that.
- take just a couple months.

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:51.810
I would say go to
counseling, go to therapy,

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:54.060
figure out who you are

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:56.190
and who you are even without the church

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:58.410
and without your wife and
without all that stuff.

00:06:58.410 --> 00:06:59.580
Once you figure all that out,

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:01.380
then you can start going
through that process

00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:04.410
of how am I gonna come out?
- Yeah, but I think he should,

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:06.960
I think the focus should be more

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:09.960
like him just finding himself,

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:10.793
you know?
- Yeah, yeah.

00:07:10.793 --> 00:07:12.240
- Like all that planning,

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:13.980
like where's he gonna
go and all that stuff,

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:15.750
yeah those are tough questions,

00:07:15.750 --> 00:07:17.460
but it doesn't have to
be answered right now

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:19.992
because it takes baby steps.

00:07:19.992 --> 00:07:20.825
(air whooshing)

00:07:20.825 --> 00:07:21.658
- [Director] Awesome.

00:07:27.529 --> 00:07:29.250
(tense music)

00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:31.860
- Coming out is not ripping off a bandaid.

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:33.630
It comes with so much anxiety.

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:37.020
It comes with so much fallbacks

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:38.640
depending on who you are,

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:40.050
where your community is aligned,

00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:41.010
you know what I mean?

00:07:41.010 --> 00:07:42.360
And it shouldn't just be ripped off.

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:44.190
'Cause even ripping off bandaids hurt.

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:45.023
You know what I mean,

00:07:45.023 --> 00:07:46.230
it's not a painless process

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:47.490
just because it's quick.

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:49.927
And people really need to understand that.

00:07:49.927 --> 00:07:52.594
(pensive music)

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:55.950
- [Director] Was there
anything in the discussion

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:58.473
that caught your attention in some way?

00:07:59.744 --> 00:08:03.510
- I think when they were
mentioning when you come out

00:08:03.510 --> 00:08:07.053
right now, that person will
show their true colors to me,

00:08:07.053 --> 00:08:09.390
that resonated with me
because that is true.

00:08:09.390 --> 00:08:11.127
The other issue that was brought up

00:08:11.127 --> 00:08:14.310
was the point of counseling
and kind of preparing myself.

00:08:14.310 --> 00:08:16.722
I feel like that could be beneficial.

00:08:16.722 --> 00:08:19.305
(tense music)

00:08:22.719 --> 00:08:24.750
- [Mary Anne] To me, I think
there was too much discussion

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:25.890
of what's step 10.

00:08:25.890 --> 00:08:27.180
What step seven?
- Yeah.

00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:28.390
- [Mary Anne] What do we
do three stages from now?

00:08:28.390 --> 00:08:29.700
- Yeah, I think-
- Yeah.

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:30.533
- that's what he's gonna get.

00:08:30.533 --> 00:08:32.530
I think what he needs from us is comfort.

00:08:33.390 --> 00:08:34.500
- [Adam] Ultimately at the end of the day,

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:35.640
people are gonna be people

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:37.410
and you can't predict how
someone's gonna react.

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:38.790
- Right.
- Also I've met people

00:08:38.790 --> 00:08:41.040
who've been in a dangerous
situation 'cause they came out.

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:42.259
- [Chris] So the biggest concern

00:08:42.259 --> 00:08:43.708
is his safety.
- Find community.

00:08:43.708 --> 00:08:46.291
(tense music)

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:49.770
- So one thing we talked about

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:51.990
was not necessarily needing a plan

00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:53.790
because your dilemma isn't coming out

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:54.840
to the world right now

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:57.660
but it's coming out to
your wife, your partner.

00:08:57.660 --> 00:09:00.123
And just as a married man of faith,

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:03.030
you said your wife grew
up in the church with you

00:09:03.030 --> 00:09:04.140
and you grew up in the church,

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:06.240
and so your wife possesses those fruits

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:08.880
of the spirit that are
like patience and kindness.

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:11.010
And I think those
attributes, like you said,

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:12.690
it sounds like are in her,

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:15.840
and so she would be loving
and kind and patient with you.

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:19.200
- One of the things I want
to just encourage you on

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:22.590
is that you've been in a
vulnerable position before

00:09:22.590 --> 00:09:25.260
where you had to put
your whole trust in God

00:09:25.260 --> 00:09:26.820
and he came through.

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:29.970
So I just encourage you
to sometimes be okay

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:32.190
with taking just the first step forward

00:09:32.190 --> 00:09:34.449
and everything else you could
figure out along the way.

00:09:34.449 --> 00:09:35.282
(air whooshing)
(tone beeps)

00:09:35.282 --> 00:09:38.640
- So I first wanna be clear
that yes, you should come out

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:40.560
but you should definitely wait

00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:42.330
and give it a little bit more time.

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:44.430
'Cause we're worried about
your safety number one.

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:46.740
The other thing too is
that you need resources

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:48.390
and you need time to get those resources.

00:09:48.390 --> 00:09:51.480
Like I said, like these divorce
processes and everything,

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:52.770
they don't take a week.

00:09:52.770 --> 00:09:54.780
And then it's all about
your community, right?

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:57.960
Personally, me and my
family is super religious

00:09:57.960 --> 00:10:01.710
so I very much understand
where you're coming from

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:03.990
about investing so much
time in your community

00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:06.600
and the sense of loss that comes with it.

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:08.640
But you have to understand
that you'll be fine,

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:10.290
your relationship with God will be fine,

00:10:10.290 --> 00:10:11.850
but this is a very tough decision

00:10:11.850 --> 00:10:15.180
that is more than that.
(tense music)

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:18.183
- [Director] Jacob, how
are you feeling right now?

00:10:20.070 --> 00:10:21.840
- [Jacob] I'm feeling like I got

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:26.840
a lot of helpful words have helped me

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:29.220
kind of put together an idea

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:31.440
of what I wanna do going forward.

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:32.760
- [Director] Have you made a decision

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:33.910
in your mind right now?

00:10:35.199 --> 00:10:36.882
- Yeah, I think I have.

00:10:36.882 --> 00:10:41.882
(pensive music)
(clock ticking)

00:11:02.233 --> 00:11:04.466
Yeah, so I'm getting home.
(gentle music)

00:11:04.466 --> 00:11:07.199
I told my wife that I
wanted do counseling.

00:11:07.199 --> 00:11:10.050
And we've been meeting
with a wonderful counselor

00:11:10.050 --> 00:11:12.240
and she has just been able to give us

00:11:12.240 --> 00:11:14.670
a lot of tools to work with.

00:11:14.670 --> 00:11:15.870
We meet one on one

00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:18.253
so I get a chance to be very open with her

00:11:18.253 --> 00:11:20.098
about how I feel.

00:11:20.098 --> 00:11:21.889
So I think within the next few months,

00:11:21.889 --> 00:11:25.530
definitely I'll be ready to fully come out

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:27.620
and just prepare myself

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:29.370
and my wife for that.

00:11:36.656 --> 00:11:38.677
I feel like the weight's
been lifted a bit.

00:11:38.677 --> 00:11:41.340
You know, I still have
a journey to go through

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:43.800
and it's gonna be hard either way.

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:48.150
But I feel a bit of closure in the sense

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:49.750
that I know what I wanna do now.

00:11:51.330 --> 00:11:53.220
Well, I do believe that it's a decision

00:11:53.220 --> 00:11:54.780
to make faithfully through God.

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:58.110
I also think that it should
be a decision that's made

00:11:58.110 --> 00:11:59.903
with the help of a counselor.

00:11:59.903 --> 00:12:02.333
I think that it's only fair to my wife

00:12:02.333 --> 00:12:03.166
that when I come out,

00:12:03.166 --> 00:12:05.790
I do it in a way that's
not only safe for me,

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:06.960
but safe for her

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:10.410
and to make sure that I
have the resources I need

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:12.303
in case something does go wrong.

00:12:14.618 --> 00:12:16.238
(Jacob laughing)

00:12:16.238 --> 00:12:18.000
Thank you.
- So proud of you.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:18.955
- Yeah.
- You guys are

00:12:18.955 --> 00:12:22.007
the first people I've ever
opened up to about this

00:12:22.007 --> 00:12:23.833
so it was...

00:12:23.833 --> 00:12:26.580
- I know that if you hit
that wall of just like

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:28.260
I don't feel like no
one's gonna support me,

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:29.093
no one has my back,

00:12:29.093 --> 00:12:30.630
know that we have your back.

00:12:30.630 --> 00:12:33.150
You know, in spirit, from the distance,

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:35.070
you have people who believe in you

00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:36.747
and who's gonna support you,

00:12:36.747 --> 00:12:39.007
and who want you to be
happy and you deserve that.

00:12:39.007 --> 00:12:39.840
[Levels] Yeah.

